House to church
Tower to drain
Voices linked in a perfect chain
Every slip, every room, every hymn, every break
Like the whole dead town was a shape in the making

Not random fear
Not random grief
Not a simple curse
Not a wandering thief
The pattern curved where the oldest homes stood
Then bent toward the spring like it knew it would

Antoni looked sick when the lines touched through
Said this was not growth, this was something new
Then Maeve found one point dead center marked
Right where the first chapel burned into dark

