But when the smoke clears from the deck—
it’s you caught in your own tech.

Chains lock tight around your wrists,
Cameras zoom on your resist.
For the first time in this place,
terror’s on the host’s own face.

[Pre-Chorus 2 – Energy 78 | drums heavier, momentum]

We hear the cables strain above,
Your laughter cracks, stripped of its love.
If we want this round to end,
we stop seeing you as god—
just a clown that breaks, like men.

[Drop / Break – Energy 100 | EDM smash, clown panic]

[DROP: distorted bass, alarm sirens, chopped crowd chants]

(Clown, panicked, glitching)
“CUT THE FEED! RESET THE GAME!
I-I’M THE STAR—REMEMBER NAME!”

(Shadow voice, cold)
“no resets.
dance, little pawn.”

Beat slams harder as chains jerk him up.

[Bridge – Energy 94 | half-time showdown, couple united]

Spotlights burn you from within,
