We stand center, hand in hand,
no more shaking at commands.

Me: “Who’s laughing now?”
You: “NOT THE CLOWN.”
Crowd (turning): “LET HIM DOWN.”

(Shadow voice, rising)
“this was never
his
crown.”

Lights flicker, higher shadow stretches over all of them.

[Final Chorus – Energy 98 | triumphant but still dark]

Clown ch-ch-checkmate—
we turn your circus into cage.
Clown ch-ch-checkmate—
we write you out of your own stage.
Clown ch-ch-checkmate—
every trick becomes our blade.
If we want to walk out free,
we make you choke on rules you made.

(tag, layered)
Lead: Checkmate…
Boyfriend: Game over, clown…
Shadow (quiet): “one piece down.
board still mine.”

[Outro – Energy 10 | crowd murmur twisting, hint of next villain]

Audience cheer bends into static,
Clown’s mic dies, scene dramatic.

(System voice)
“HOST STATUS: NEUTRALIZED.
DIRECTOR STATUS:
RED-ACTED.”

(Shadow whisper, alone)
“your move,
players.”

Single chess-clock tick. Silence.',
