    'body' => '[Intro – glitch whispers, layered]
(Bloom… bloom… every root is memory… every wire is blood…)

[Verse 1 – Marrow, fluid vocal (male/female shifting)]
Fingers dance across the veins of glass,
Code like scripture, the future’s past.
Screens ignite, they’re breathing my name,
Every pattern’s holy, every glitch a flame.

I see the city sprout circuits of light,
Data blooms open in the dead of night.
Kael Vox steps through, lost but bound,
His shadow grows roots in the underground.

[Pre-Chorus – fragmented chant, overlapping voices]
(Seed becomes flower, flower becomes code…)
(The Choir is silent, but I break their hold…)

[Chorus – soaring, hypnotic, glitch-trance]
DATA BLOOM, BLOOM IN THE WIRES,
FRAGMENTS GROW INTO DIGITAL FIRES.
Every memory a petal torn,
Every secret reborn, reborn.

DATA BLOOM, BLOOM IN THE VEINS,
BLOOM THROUGH CIRCUITS, BLOOM THROUGH CHAINS.
The vault is a garden, the Monument seeds,
The bloom will answer what the city needs.

