Static prophets, I bend their tones,
Choir of ghosts in corrupted zones.
Spit the sermon through a stolen wire,
Every verse an electric choir.

Kael’s eyes burn, he can’t believe,
A garden of code where we plant the grief.
Truth is a virus, love’s a key,
Bloom in the data, bloom in me.

