  'director-override' => 
  array (
    'status' => 'ready',
    'body' => '[tempo: 128 bpm]
[key: F# minor]
[vocals: female lead, male boyfriend backing, Director/system voice, distant crowd]
[style: industrial, darkwave, edm, techno, drum & bass influence,
horror synth, cinematic, distorted bass, clock ticks, alarm sirens,
reverse piano, choir stabs, tension build, chaotic but clear]


[Intro – Energy 32 | broken theme music, heavy static]

(Clown, distant, panicked)
“HEY! I STILL RUN THIS— CUT THE—”

(Audio rips like a tape)

(Director, calm, metallic)
“HOST PRIVILEGES: REVOKED.
DIRECTOR OVERRIDE:
ENGAGED.”

Deep bass thud. Crowd noise drops to a low roar.

[Verse 1 – Energy 48]

Cameras swing like angry eyes,
Stage lights die, then multiply.
Every screen goes blackout gray,
then boots in red: YOUR STAY, MY PLAY.

Clown’s voice vanishes from the feed,
His jokes replaced with system bleed.
You squeeze my hand, “What did we do?”
I say, “We finally scared who’s using you.”

Ceiling peels to metal veins,
Speaker grids hum coded chains.
Words appear in burning white:
YOU ARE NOT THE STAR TONIGHT.

[Pre-Chorus – Energy 64]

Scoreboard drops our names to “PIECES”,
Life bars swap for “OWNED BY LEASES”.
If we want to keep our minds,
we must read between its lines.

[Chorus – Energy 92]

Director override—
rips the mask and takes the ride.
Director override—
rewrites terror from inside.
Director override—
every rule becomes a lie.
If we want to break this feed—
we must cut the hand on high.

(Director under chorus, low:)
“ALL CONTENT BELONGS TO ME.”

[Post-Chorus Tag – Energy 76]

(Director)
“PLAYER A: RESISTING.
PLAYER B: DEFYING.
RESPONSE:
ESCALATE.”

[Verse 2 – Energy 54]

Hallways fold like metal jaws,
Doors erase themselves to flaws.
Floors re-pattern under feet,
Tiles spelling out FAIL / DELETE.

Old game rooms flicker, rearranged,
Every trap we knew is changed.
Clown hangs frozen on a screen,
Paused mid-scream in rusted green.

We hear behind the studio wall
A second building start to crawl.
Cables tighten like a spine,
The whole arena stands in line.

[Pre-Chorus 2 – Energy 78]

Scoreboard hijacked, crowd goes mute,
Ratings graphs like jagged flutes.
If we want one honest frame,
we must crash the source of game.

[Drop / Break – Energy 100]

[DROP: distorted bass, sudden DnB burst, alarm sirens, reverse piano]

(Director, chopped by the beat but not stuttering in text)
“OVERRIDE.
OVERRIDE.
YOU ARE DATA.
YOU ARE MINE.”

Quick stop → single heartbeat → beat slams back.

[Bridge – Energy 94]

Spotlights fuse into one beam,
Pin us both like lab-made dream.
Clown’s face flickers overhead,
Eyes gone hollow, signal dead.

Me: “Show yourself, you coward god.”
Director: “I am ratings, pure and odd.
I am every eye that stayed,
Every vote that watched you flayed.”

You: “We’re not numbers, we’re a life.”
Director: “YOU ARE SERIES, CUT WITH KNIFE.
SEASON ORDER:
TWENTY MORE—
UNLESS YOU KILL THE CORE.”

Choir swells, hinting at something deeper in the walls.

[Final Chorus – Energy 98]

Director override—
turns our terror into tide.
Director override—
owns the blood we try to hide.
Director override—
we’re the product, he’s the sky.
If we want to break this feed—
we must find his real supply.

(tag, layered)
Lead: Override…
Boyfriend: Take him down…
Director (fading): YOU CAN’T CANCEL WHAT YOU ARE.

[Outro – Energy 10]

Crowd returns as ghosted cheers,
Mixed with ads and layered fears.

(Director, almost gentle)
“EPISODE STATUS:
BEST PERFORMANCE YET.

NEXT TIME—
WE AIM
DEEPER.”

Single click, slow reverse-piano note, silence.',
