    'body' => '[INTRO female whisper close mic icy arps low sub faint road noise distant choir]
Stay where I can reach you
Stay where I still know your name
Do not walk into that warmth
Like it was meant for you

[VERSE 1 female fast rap low calm conversational half time drums deep sub restrained industrial pulse]
June found the back door open to the frost
Mud on the steps and one glove lost
Maris said they did not run
They were led by something soft

No broken room, no sign of force
Just one chair turned toward the north
A cup still warm, a coat half gone
And that same low note inside the walls

Cal checked tracks where the gravel bent
Toward the road by the dead rail fence
Ezra looked tired, more than mad
Like he knew this was the part he feared

Antoni held the old page shut
Said do not call too loud out there
If they hear your love in the wrong key
It will use it

[PRE CHORUS female lead whispered opera swell male ghost harmony choir rise]
It leaves the door
It leaves the light
It wants the chase
It wants the night

[CHORUS female lead huge cathedral hook male stack eerie harmony choir stabs]
Follow the warmth
Follow the glow
Before the soft voice says do not go
Follow the breath
Follow the trace
Before the choir learns their face

Follow the warmth
Down the line
Through the cold fields and the warning signs
If we lose them here
We lose more than one
We lose the part that still turns back

[VERSE 2 female fast rap tighter cadence icy arp pulse low percussion]
Roadside chapel ruin, culvert, trees
Every stop held that hush like sleep
Then Maeve saw movement by the frozen creek
One figure still and one more shape beneath

June stepped first with her hands out wide
Said come with me, do not close your eyes
They turned half back and for one short breath
They almost looked like them again

Then the second shape rose from the dark
Not claws, not rage, just a steady calm
A hood, a glow, a hand on a shoulder
Like grief itself had learned to guide

Maris whispered do not look at it long
Ezra said now, break the line, move on
But the slipped one smiled through tears and said
I was cold until it found me

[PRE CHORUS female whisper close mic choir pressure slow rise]
It gives a path
