Courier running but the streets don’t change,
Every turn bleeds neon strange.
Pulse in my chest but it’s not my own,
City’s beat rewrote my bones.
Nyra’s voice cuts through the static,
Soft but deadly, pure and tragic.
Kaelith hunts with venom eyes,
Dr. Vox lies in coded skies.

[Pre-Chorus – glitch echo, layered voices]
Fragments fall, I can’t decide,
Who I am and what I hide.

[Chorus – trance surge, cinematic hardwave]
Fragments of the self, tearing apart,
Monsters move in rhythm with my heart.
Every piece I lose, another cost,
Fragments of the self — what’s left gets lost.

[Verse 2 – rap, darker tone]
Syndicate chains burn through my skin,
Game too deep, I can’t win.
I was a courier, simple beat,
Now I’m a ghost the city eats.
Nyra’s song — betrayal or prayer,
Dr. Vox whispers, “you’re not there.”
L’Ren smiles from a throne unseen,
Every pawn caught in her machine.

[Bridge – crooner overlay, orchestral rise]
Am I music, am I code?
Am I lost on this haunted road?
Every fragment screams my name,
But none of them feel the same.

[Chorus – extended, glitch distortion]
Fragments of the self, tearing apart,
Monsters move in rhythm with my heart.
Every piece I lose, another cost,
Fragments of the self — what’s left gets lost.

[Outro – lo-fi fade, static whisper]
(Fragment… fragment… gone.)',
