  'holographic-ghosts-chapter-18' => 
  array (
    'status' => 'ready',
    'body' => '[Intro – ghostly choirs, faint radio hiss]
(We are the voices… we are the lost…)

[Verse 1 – Kael, hushed male vocal]
Figures flicker in electric flame,
Every whisper repeats my name.
Faces stolen, lives denied,
But their ghosts refuse to hide.

Children cry in binary streams,
Lovers drown in broken dreams.
Every loss the Monument claimed,
Every ghost still knows my name.

[Chorus – soaring, ethereal yet heavy]
HOLOGRAPHIC GHOSTS, FILL THE SKY,
DIGITAL SPIRITS REFUSE TO DIE.
Every soul the Reset stole,
Still alive in the Monument’s soul.

HOLOGRAPHIC GHOSTS, CALL TO ME,
SET US FREE OR LET IT BE.
I bleed the circuit, I burn the cost,
I hold the weight of all who are lost.

[Verse 2 – Lucienne, ghostly female vocal]
Kael, my love, the fire was real,
But I was the wound that would never heal.
Your scar was forged from the death of flame,
But I remained inside the name.

[Kael, answering]
Lucienne’s face in light’s decay,
Alive in code but stripped away.
If I free the dead, I free her too,
But will I survive if I break this truth?

[Bridge – ghost choir, overlapping voices]
(Kael Vox, we are your sin…
Kael Vox, let us in…
Kael Vox, release the chain…
Kael Vox, remember the flame…)

