    'status' => 'ready',
    'body' => 'This is your boarding call
No bags, no fear
Only the beat
Only the year

Stamps on my heart, dust on my shoes
New city, same bruise, same truth

I got miles in my eyes, and a spark in my throat
I keep love like a lighter in a rain soaked coat
Rich lights flash, poor streets breathe
Middle of the map, that’s me
I don’t want perfect, I want loud
I want the night to shake the crowd
I want a moment that doesn’t explain
Just hits my ribs like a moving train

One hand up, one hand on my chest
If this is the end, make it the best

Midnight passport, stamp my soul
New year heat in a blackout glow
We don’t need answers, we need a drop
Hold me tight when the world won’t stop
Midnight passport, take my name
Throw it high in the neon flame
If love is chaos, I want the proof
Right here, right now, under this roof

Airport prayers and hostel laughs
Broken plans and perfect halves
Kissed on bridges, cried in trains
Danced through loss to kill the pain
I learned the rich can still feel empty
I learned the poor can still feel plenty
And me, I’m stuck in the in between
Trying to live like I mean the dream

New year, new miles, same heartbeat thump
City lights jump when the kick drum jump
I don’t chase clout, I chase that spark
I chase that love in the loud and dark
Suit on the balcony, kid on the curb
Both want mercy, both want words
I’m in the middle, I feel it all
So when the bass hits, I don’t fall

Say it
Say it
Now

Midnight passport, stamp my soul
New year heat in a blackout glow
Hands up, no fear, let it pop
If we break, let it break on top
Midnight passport, take my name
Throw it high in the neon flame
If love is chaos, I want the proof
Right here, right now, under this roof

If tomorrow asks what I became
Tell it I chose the fire, not the blame
Tell it I stopped counting scars
And started counting stars

