Turn my silence into violent drums
I came to disappear, I stayed to see
What the night pulls out of me
Kathmandu, don’t let the signal die
I want a sign in a dirty sky
If I break, let the mountain know
I was here, I was here, I was whole

Black incense, black incense
Don’t fade out, don’t fade out

Bells ring soft like a warning wire
Every step got a hidden fire
Rooftop laughs in a private glow
Street kids run where the cold winds blow
A monk walks past with eyes like stone
Makes me feel how far I’ve roamed
I’m not saved, I’m not damned, I’m just awake
Learning what a hard city can take

No clean answer, no clean name
Just a pulse that survives the flame
Say it with thunder

