    'body' => '[tempo: 124 bpm]
N O E X I T A R C A D E:
THE CLOWN GAME SHOW!”

[impact hit, crowd roar, sirens]

[Verse 1 – Energy 46 | female lead, half-rap, tight drums, horror synth]
Neon buzz at the end of the street,
Rain on the sign, bl-blood in the beat.
Line of contestants, nervous smiles,
Fine print contracts eight pages of trials.
They stamp our wrists with barcode ink,
Cameras track every flinch and blink.
You joke, “At least the prizes glow,”
Then the doors slam shut and the lights drop low.
Floor lights flicker like a heart attack,
Stage spins up, no turning back.
One spotlight burns our faces white—
the clown walks in and k-k-kills the night.

[Pre-Chorus – Energy 62 | rising synths, snare build, subtle glitch vox]
Rules roll out on the ceiling screens,
Red font chewing through our dreams:
“ONE LIFE EACH. NO TIMEOUT.
EVERY ROUND, SOMEBODY’S OUT.”
You grip my hand and hiss, “Stay close,”
But we’re already o-owned by the host.

[Chorus – Energy 90 | huge anthemic hook, sidechain bass, crowd chants, glitch edges]
Welcome to the n-no exit arcade—
where the clown turns fear into trade.
Welcome to the cl-cl-clown game show—
every scream makes ratings grow.
Welcome to the n-no exit arcade—
flash of teeth and loaded plays.
If you want to walk back home,
prove you’re w-worth the blood we’ve paid.
“LAUGH OR DIE, KIDS! L-LAUGH OR DIE!”

[Post-Chorus Tag – Energy 74 | fx stabs, call-and-response]

[Crowd chant – processed]
“ONE MORE ROUND! NO WAY BACK!
“EMERGENCY EXITS:
DECORATION ONLY.”

[low boom, ticking resumes]

[Verse 2 – Energy 54 | heavier drums, more movement, glitch stabs on key words]
First game: four doors, all the same,
Each one branded with our names.
“PICK A PATH,” the clown half-sings,
“LOSE YOUR NERVE OR LOSE SOME THINGS.”
He tosses keys in a metal bowl,
Every clink like a st-st-stolen soul.
We hear gears grinding in the walls,
Hidden saws and hidden falls.
He smells like greasepaint, rust and smoke,
Smiles so wide the skin looks broke.
But when the cameras pan too high,
We see dark wires in the sky.
Something else tugs at his feet,
Pulls his shadow off the seat.
He’s not god, just painted meat—
but we don’t know that y-y-yet on this first week.

[Pre-Chorus 2 – Energy 76 | tom build, tension rise, glitch delays]
Scoreboard wakes with a hungry glow,
Life bars lined like throats in a row.
If we want to beat this night,
we must learn the rules they hide.

[Bridge – Energy 94 | half-time, cinematic, call-and-response]
Steel catwalks overhead,
