This is how the story starts—
before the sequels, before the scars.
Me (lead): “Is this real or is it staged?”
You (male backing): “Either way, we’re in the cage.”
Clown bows low with rotten grace,
Painted tears on a r-r-rotting face.
Clown: “YOU SIGNED UP FOR ALL THIS FUN.
ONLY RULE—
NO ONE RUNS.”

[Crowd chant – stomp rhythm]
“NO ONE RUNS. NO ONE RUNS.”

[Final Chorus – Energy 98 | max power, octave-up doubles, glitch emphasis on title]
Welcome to the n-no exit arcade—
where the clown turns fear into trade.
Welcome to the cl-cl-clown game show—
every scream makes ratings grow.
Welcome to the n-no exit arcade—
once you’re in, your fate is played.
If you ever see that sign,
turn around—
or l-l-lose your name.


(Tag – stacked)
Lead: No exit…
Crowd: NO WAY OUT.
Clown (fading, pitch-bent): S-SEE YOU NEXT EPISODE…

[Outro – Energy 8 | ticking, broken theme, tape hiss]

Theme music plays from a broken tape,
Warps like metal trying to escape.

(System voice – soft, distant)
“EPISODE ONE:
COMPLETE.

CONCLUSION:
THEY’LL BE BACK.”

Single coin drop.
One last distorted clown chuckle, then silence.',
