Sing in the crackle of the phantom choir.

[Pre-Chorus – rising static, overlapping whispers]
(Frequency bending… silence descending…)
(Do not listen… do not listen…)

[Chorus – explosive wall of sound, distorted chants]
PHANTOM FREQUENCY, BLEEDING MY SKIN,
ECHOES OF TRUTH THAT I CAN’T KEEP IN.
Every whisper claws, every ghost consumes,
Every secret howls inside this room.

PHANTOM FREQUENCY, TEAR ME APART,
SIGNALS OF FIRE IN THE DEPTH OF MY HEART.
The Choir can’t bind what the static frees,
I’m chained forever to phantom frequencies.

[Verse 2 – Kael, frantic flow with rap overlay]
Fractals bloom on the broken screen,
Images split where the wires convene.
I see the Reset, flames in glass,
I see my hands in the shattered past.

Every scream is a code I know,
Every ghost is a seed I sow.
Marrow begs me to shut it down,
But the phantom signal wears the crown.

[Bridge 1 – Lucienne’s voice, angelic but glitching]
(Kael… listen… through the static storm…)
(Kael… remember… the night it was born…)
Her voice cuts sharp through the binary rain,
A memory alive in electric pain.

Luci (sung, broken):
You lit the fire, you struck the spark,
You sealed the Monument, left it dark.
I loved the man, but the city burned,
Kael, your memory will be returned.

[Chorus 2 – larger, more chaotic]
PHANTOM FREQUENCY, BURSTING THROUGH GLASS,
SECRETS UNEARTHED FROM THE MONUMENT’S PAST.
Every word is a nail in the skin of time,
Every voice is a crime, a crime.

PHANTOM FREQUENCY, BLEEDING THE SKY,
THOUSAND DEAD FACES BEGIN TO CRY.
No silence left, no signal dies,
The phantom lives where the Choir lies.

[Verse 3 – Kael, broken, whisper-rap mix]
I fall to the floor as the static feeds,
Every prayer becomes a seed.
Lucienne’s ghost in the radio glow,
A voice I lost forty years ago.

The Hollow’s breath is in the hum,
A mirrored face where the signals run.
Did I betray or did I obey?
Did I burn the world or lead the way?

[Bridge 2 – The Phantom Frequency itself, voice layered with Choir]
(Kael Vox… you are the flame…
Kael Vox… you bear the blame…
