Old town glow in a champagne mist
Tourists laugh like the world won’t twist
But the river keeps a darker truth
It carries vows and broken youth
Rich tables sparkle, velvet warm
Street hands shake in the winter storm
And me, I’m stuck in the in between
Chasing a sign in a gothic scene

One more breath, then leap
Let the night speak

Prague, you’re a beautiful warning
