  'rain-in-chrome-alley-chapter-3' => 
  array (
    'status' => 'ready',
    'body' => '[Intro – vintage crackle, crooner echo]
Rain falls heavy in Chrome Alley…
Neon signs blur like memories I can’t carry.
Shadows flicker, I hear the hum,
Something’s watching, but I can’t run.

[Verse 1 – slow rap, steady, cinematic]
Boots hit puddles, rhythm to the night,
City bleeds color under broken lights.
Every corner whispers names I lost,
Every shortcut comes with a cost.
Jacket soaked, saxophone case,
Monsters in windows with no face.
I move quiet, but the streets still know,
The Courier’s beat where the acid flows.

[Pre-Chorus – glitch voice, layered whispers]
Rain on metal, heart on fire,
Static sings through broken wire.
I walk alone but I feel the stare,
Eyes in the shadows everywhere.

[Chorus – synthwave swell]
Rain in Chrome Alley, dripping steel and fear,
Voices in the static only I can hear.
Monsters move silent, teeth in disguise,
Rain in Chrome Alley where the city lies.

[Verse 2 – rap, darker tone]
Passing faces with circuits for skin,
A reptile grin where the night begins.
Graffiti bleeds in ultraviolet tones,
Warning signs carved into stone.
Every raindrop tastes like rust,
Every handshake breaks my trust.
Whispers deal data like contraband,
A signal burns hot in my shaking hand.

[Bridge – crooner vocal overlay, orchestral build]
I thought it was thunder, but it was a scream,
I thought it was real, but it’s just a dream.
Blood in the gutter turns violet blue,
Chrome Alley hides the truth from you.

[Chorus – extended, trance beat rising]
Rain in Chrome Alley, dripping steel and fear,
Voices in the static only I can hear.
Monsters move silent, teeth in disguise,
Rain in Chrome Alley where the city lies.

Rain in Chrome Alley, heartbeat underground,
Every step I take is another sound.
This city’s alive, but it don’t forgive,
Rain in Chrome Alley — you die or you live.

[Verse 3 – spoken word, glitch distortion]
Drip, drip, drip — the city bleeds slow,
Monsters smile where the shadows grow.
I don’t belong here, I never did,
But Chrome Alley don’t care, it keeps what it hid.
Every echo another ghost in my ear,
Every neon light burns cold with fear.
I play my song but the notes don’t stay,
They fade in the acid — washed away.

[Outro – lo-fi fade, whisper layers]
Rain in Chrome Alley…
Neon sighs, monsters tally…
Courier’s beat, heartbeat hollow…
Rain in Chrome Alley — nowhere to follow.',
