    'body' => 'Lyrics (long)
[Intro – vintage crackle, crooner tone]
Her voice cuts soft, but the world obeys,
Crown of shadows, throne of haze.

[Verse 1 – slow rap, heavy beat]
Queen of wires, Queen of bone,
Rules a city that’s never her own.
Monsters kneel, Kaelith bows,
Every life chained to her vows.
Courier stands but my knees go weak,
Her will is steel, her words don’t speak.
Static sings in the palace dome,
I’m not free — I’m never home.

[Pre-Chorus – glitch whispers]
Her law in my blood, her hand on my fate,
Every breath is another weight.

[Chorus – cinematic swell]
The Alien Queen’s demand, no choice, no say,
Her crown burns bright, the city decays.
Obey her voice or vanish in dust,
The Alien Queen demands our trust.

[Verse 2 – faster rap, intensity]
Nyra shakes with a haunted tone,
Her song enslaved, her voice not her own.
Dr. Vox flickers on broken screens,
Says “truth don’t matter, it’s just what she means.”
Kaelith grins with a predator’s stare,
His loyalty lives but his soul ain’t there.
Courier’s beat against the wall,
If I don’t kneel, I’ll lose it all.

[Bridge – crooner + orchestral build]
She don’t bleed, she don’t break,
Every vow she makes is fake.
Still I rise, still I stand,
I won’t bow to the Syndicate’s hand.

[Chorus – extended, trance surge]
The Alien Queen’s demand, no choice, no say,
Her crown burns bright, the city decays.
Obey her voice or vanish in dust,
The Alien Queen demands our trust.

[Outro – lo-fi fade, whispered glitch]
(The Queen… commands…)
Obey… or die.

