We broke the ring
We split the seam
We kept one part of us unseen

The choir remains
That is the scar
Not every light comes back to where we are
Not every name walks out intact
Not every soul we loved comes all the way back

The choir remains
But so do we
Cut in the throat, not down on our knees
And somewhere far beyond this spring
A colder room begins to sing

[OUTRO female whisper with distant male ghost, nylon guitar fingerpicking, tape delay fade]
No bell now
No fire now
Just one thin tone
Still alive',
