    'body' => '[Intro – glass chime + whispering layers]
(Vault of echoes… vault of names… every pane a different flame…)

[Verse 1 – Kael, steady but haunted]
Mirrors bleed with forgotten skies,
Every version wears my eyes.
Hands of glass reach from the wall,
Some forgive and some let me fall.

Flashes of fire, faces torn,
A thousand lives I may have worn.
Am I the spark or just the ash?
Am I the Reset’s final crash?

[Pre-Chorus – layered whispers, chaotic but soft]
(Touch the pane, bleed the truth,
Every echo returns to you…)

[Chorus – soaring industrial-choir fusion]
VAULT OF ECHOES, BREAK ME IN TWO,
EVERY GLASS A WORLD I KNEW.
I see the blood, I hear the lies,
A thousand versions never die.

VAULT OF ECHOES, SHOW ME MORE,
EVERY DOOR IS ANOTHER WAR.
If one is me and all are true,
Which Kael survives when I walk through?

[Verse 2 – Kael, angrier, heavier beat]
A soldier’s oath, a traitor’s scar,
A savior crowned in electric tar.
I see Lucienne with a bloody hand,
I see Marrow burn with a stolen brand.

