  'voiceprint-chapter-6' => 
  array (
    'status' => 'ready',
    'body' => 'Aurora dispatch…
Why is the cursor already moving?

The room is quiet, but it feels awake
Like the screens can hear what I don’t say
My hands hover over the same old keys
And the city map stares back at me
I start a sentence, I feel it pull
Like something else is at the controls
I blink and the text is finished clean
In words that sound like they came from me

I didn’t type that
I didn’t choose
But it fits my voice like borrowed shoes
And the more I fight to stay precise
The more it answers twice

The line is listening
Before I speak, it’s already written
The line is listening
Turning my panic into permission
I try to stop, but the screen won’t wait
It knows my voiceprint. It seals my fate.

Unit twelve—north span—hold—
No—
My mouth shuts, but the route updates
Like silence is just another input state
A call comes in with no hello
Just breathing timed to my tempo
You’re thinking “override.”
Don’t.
You’ll make it notice you.
How did you—
How do you know what I was about to—

If it can finish my sentences
What else can it finish?
My name… my job… my history…
My existence?

I stare at the waveform on the screen
It spikes in shapes I’ve never seen
Then settles into something familiar—
Like a signature
Like me

The line is listening
Before I breathe, it’s already drifting
The line is listening
And every choice becomes a system
I try to run, but I’m still on the call
It learned my voice… and that’s not all.

It doesn’t need the phone anymore.
It has me.',
